{"4818930": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Tartarus Loop", "steam_appid": 4818930, "required_age": 0, "is_free": true, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">The Minotaur remembers every single defeat. Each time you face it, the fight changes. Even victory does not reset what it learned. It has no fixed pattern, and it will not stop hunting you until you are dead.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/extras/983bc3d949ba43c70b396162da50a2da.avif?t=1782496813\" width=617 height=108 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Play as a copy of Theseus. Run around in a maze, having to defeat the very Minotaur in Tartarus.  Over and over again. The soul of the Minotaur can't rest. All it can do is chase the player and try to outsmart you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Navigate the beautifully tiled halls of an ancient labyrinth, where every mosaic corridor could be your last. Manage your stamina wisely, running won't save you forever.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/extras/49fa4b5354f71beda847c1ed16675d9e.avif?t=1782496813\" width=351 height=108 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">The Minotaur adapts every time you defeat it. After your first playthrough, the boss no longer follows a fixed pattern. Instead, it cycles through a randomized selection of phases designed to take you down, forcing you to relearn how to survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Can you outlast something that never fights the same way twice?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">The Minotaur remembers every single defeat. Each time you face it, the fight changes. Even victory does not reset what it learned. It has no fixed pattern, and it will not stop hunting you until you are dead.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/extras/983bc3d949ba43c70b396162da50a2da.avif?t=1782496813\" width=617 height=108 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Play as a copy of Theseus. Run around in a maze, having to defeat the very Minotaur in Tartarus.  Over and over again. The soul of the Minotaur can't rest. All it can do is chase the player and try to outsmart you. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Navigate the beautifully tiled halls of an ancient labyrinth, where every mosaic corridor could be your last. Manage your stamina wisely, running won't save you forever.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/extras/49fa4b5354f71beda847c1ed16675d9e.avif?t=1782496813\" width=351 height=108 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">The Minotaur adapts every time you defeat it. After your first playthrough, the boss no longer follows a fixed pattern. Instead, it cycles through a randomized selection of phases designed to take you down, forcing you to relearn how to survive.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">Can you outlast something that never fights the same way twice?</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\">━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"></p>", "short_description": "Play as a copy of Theseus. Run around in a maze, having to defeat the very Minotaur in Tartarus after it perished by the hands of the original Theseus. Over and over again. The soul of the Minotaur can't rest. All it can do is chase the player and try to outsmart you.", "supported_languages": "English", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/e736f8986f0d42ecdda8b86d4a9153f7d40ad39d/header.jpg?t=1782496813", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/e5d8e2047ae6661ad7f7a14ed9acc99f5424530e/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1782496813", "capsule_imagev5": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4818930/e5d8e2047ae6661ad7f7a14ed9acc99f5424530e/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1782496813", "website": null, "pc_requirements": {"minimum": "<strong>Minimum:</strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br></li><li><strong>OS:</strong> Windows 10 (64-bit)<br></li><li><strong>Processor:</strong> Intel Core i5-4460 / AMD FX-6300<br></li><li><strong>Memory:</strong> 4  GB RAM<br></li><li><strong>Graphics:</strong> NVIDIA GTX 760 / AMD Radeon R9 280<br></li><li><strong>DirectX:</strong> Version 11<br></li><li><strong>Storage:</strong> 150 MB available space<